adjudication.rationale:
In apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts the auth check is:

```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
  return res.status(403)
}
```

If `CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is unset (`undefined`) and the header is also absent (`undefined`), the `!==` comparison evaluates to `false`, so the request is accepted with no authentication. Since the endpoint then parses `userId/appSlug/keys` and updates/creates credentials for that `userId`, this can expose an unauthenticated credential-overwrite path when credential sharing is enabled but the secret is not configured. The timing-unsafe aspect is also true for plain string comparison, but the critical, verifiable issue is the unset-secret bypass present in the diff.
